Z||000004||FieroJoe||10-28-2001||10:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by firstfiero:<BR><B>     Alright alright.... laugh it up....ya know what I ment!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Thanks ,The fiero store has some but I'm trying to avoid them.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Fiero Store's assorted colored $40 "leather" shift knobs are crap.  I immediatly sent it back because it was so cheap.  The leather is thinner than a shift boot's, and what it was wrapped around was similar to lathed balsa wood.  It didnt even have any threads in it, you were just to cut your own with the threads of your shifter, throwing shavings all over the place.<P>I too am looking for a stock grey shift knob, so much better than that POS from the Fiero Store.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||10-29-2001||05:02 AM||||FieroJoe--Funny you should mention that.  The 1<sup>st</sup> leather covered shift knob I got from the Fiero Store had some sort of balsa wood base.  I called and complained and they told me (what is now obviously a  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif"> story) that I must have received the one and only prototype.  The good news was that they sent me another ASAP with a plastic core.  I've had that one for a few weeks now and haven't had any thread problems.  (No problems with thin leather, either.)||||reg||1
